enic behaviour in gold-ore mill tailings, Massif Central, France: hydrogeochemical study and investigation of in situ redox signatures</article-title><source>Applied Geochemistry</source><year>2004</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>1785</fpage><lpage>1800</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.apgeochem.2004.03.012</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Harvey</surname><given-names>CF</given-names></name><name><surname>Swartz</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Badruzzaman</surname><given-names>ABM</given-names></name><name><surname>Keon-Blute</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Ali</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Jay</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Beckie</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Niedan</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Brabander</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Oates</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashfaque</surname><given-names>KN</given-names></name><name><surname>Islam</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hemond</surname><given-names>HF</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahmed</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Arsenic Mobility and Groundwater Extraction in Bangladesh</article-title><source>Science</source><year>2002</year><volume>298</volume><fpage>1602</fpage><lpage>1606</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12446905</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.1076978</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Polizzotto</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Harvey</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Badruzzman</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Ali</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Newville</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sutton</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Fendorf</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Solid-phases and desorption processes of arsenic within Bangladesh sediments</article-title><source>Chemical Geology</source><year>2006</year><volume>228</volume><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>111</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cummings</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Caccavo</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Fendorf</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenzweig</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Arsenic mobilization by the dissimilatory Fe(III)-reducing bacterium Shewanella alga BrY</article-title><source>Environmental Science &#x00026; Technology</source><year>1999</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>723</fpage><lpage>729</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/es980541c</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Langner</surname><given-names>HW</given-names></name><name><surname>Inskeep</surname><given-names>WP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Microbial reduction of arsenate in the presence of ferrihydrite</article-title><source>Environmental Science &#x00026; Technology</source><year>2000</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>3131</fpage><lpage>3136</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/es991414z</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zobrist</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dowdle</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Oremland</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mobilization of Arsenite by Dissimilatory Reduction of Adsorbed Arsenate</article-title><source>Environmental Science &#x00026; Technology</source><year>2000</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>4747</fpage><lpage>4753</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/es001068h</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van Geen</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rose</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Thoral</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Garnier</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Zheng</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Bottero</surname><given-names>JY</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Decoupling of As and Fe release to Bangladesh groundwater under reducing conditions. Part II: Evidence from sediment incubations</article-title><source>Geochimica et Cosmochimica Acta</source><year>2004</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>3475</fpage><lpage>3486</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.gca.2004.02.014</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Islam</surname><given-names>FS</given-names></name><name><surname>Gault</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Boothman</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Polya</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Charnock</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Chatterjee</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Lloyd</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of metal-reducing 